polecat-browser (1.0.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Initial release.
  * Core browsing with Qt 6 WebEngine: navigation, reload/stop, address and
    search bar.
  * Tabbed browsing and multiple windows, including private windows.
  * Session save and restore, and reopen-closed-tab support.
  * SQLite-backed bookmarks (with folders, import and export) and history
    (with search and clearing).
  * Download manager with pause/resume/cancel, safe filename handling and
    warnings for dangerous file types.
  * Private browsing via an off-the-record WebEngine profile; private activity
    is never persisted.
  * GNOME-inspired interface: header bar, navigation toolbar, tab strip,
    collapsible sidebar, light/dark/system theme.
  * Privacy controls: third-party cookie blocking, HTTPS-only mode,
    Do Not Track, per-site permissions, clear-browsing-data.
  * Optional content blocking from bundled filter lists with a user allowlist.
  * Optional study tools: reader mode, notes, vocabulary, reading list,
    focus timer and a translation helper.
  * Debian packaging (.deb only) with desktop file, metainfo and icon.

 -- OpentiaOS Developer <opentiaos@gmail.com>  Thu, 01 Jan 2026 00:00:00 +0530
